   Chicago, IL, APR 07-10, 2005},
Organization = {Midwest Polit Sci Assoc},
Abstract = {We provide an introduction to the regression discontinuity design (RDD)
   and use the technique to evaluate models of sequential Senate elections
   predicting that the winning party for one Senate seat will receive fewer
   votes in the next election for the other seat. Using data on U.S. Senate
   elections from 1946 to 2004, we find strong evidence that the outcomes
   of the elections for the two Senate seats are independent.},
