Volume = {39},
Number = {1},
Pages = {3-21},
Month = {FEB},
Abstract = {This introduction and the articles that follow are motivated by three
   main goals. First, they elaborate and promote a comparative approach to
   the study of international legal institutions. Second, they seek to
   better understand the role of courts in transforming international and
   domestic governance. Finally, the central aim of the issue is to examine
   how the legalization of global politics may be linked to changes in
   democratic participation. The overarching aim is to examine the factors
   shaping when and how courts may serve as arenas for citizen
   participation leading to important political, legal, and social
   developments. This introductory article provides a testable framework
   elaborating both the opportunities and limitations of this dynamic for
   democratic politics.},
